# Deliberately narrow. There is no `* text=auto` here, because adding one would
# renormalise every file in the repository and bury a real change in a diff
# nobody can read.
#
# These entries exist for one reason: this repository is developed on Windows
# with core.autocrlf enabled, and a checkout there rewrites LF to CRLF. That is
# harmless for Python and Markdown, and fatal for the files below — a Dockerfile
# whose `RUN cmd \` continuations end in CRLF leaks a carriage return into the
# shell, and the build fails with an error that names none of this. Pinning eol=lf
# means a Windows checkout produces files that still build on Linux.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch line endings, never try to diff as text.
*.pptx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
